<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-10228] Start multiple caches in parallel may lead to the fact that some of the caches won&apos;t be registered.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10228</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;It looks like the root cause of the issue is that&#160;&lt;tt&gt;CacheGroupContext.addCacheContext()&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;(which is called in parallel) does not use a lock/semaphore in order to synchronize&#160;&lt;tt&gt;caches&lt;/tt&gt; updates.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;private&lt;/span&gt; void addCacheContext(GridCacheContext cctx) {
    ArrayList&amp;lt;GridCacheContext&amp;gt; caches = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; ArrayList&amp;lt;&amp;gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;.caches);

    &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt; add = caches.add(cctx);

    ...

    &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;.caches = caches;
}

&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The possible workaround is to disable parallel start of caches by setting the&#160;&lt;tt&gt;IGNITE_ALLOW_START_CACHES_IN_PARALLEL&lt;/tt&gt; property to &lt;tt&gt;false&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
